From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: text services answer ITextServices2 and ITextDocument2

Microsoft 365 Word, once signed in with a work account, ended in a
fail-fast (exception 0x02784198, from mso20win32client) as soon as it
showed its start screen, and later whenever a new document opened. The
start screen is drawn by Office's React Native layer, and its text box
("Describe the document you'd like to write") is a windowless RichEdit:
it looks up IID_ITextServices2 in the RichEdit DLL (Wine's riched20 is
loaded in place of Office's own copy), asks the text services for
ITextServices2 and ITextDocument2, and draws with TxDrawD2D. None of the
three existed, and Office treats each as fatal.

Now riched20 (and msftedit, which forwards to it) exports
IID_ITextServices2; the text services object answers ITextServices2 (the
same object: ITextServices with TxGetNaturalSize2, which also gives the
first line's ascent, and TxDrawD2D) and ITextDocument2 (its ITextDocument
part is the existing document interface; the later methods keep the
caret type, notification mode, typography and math options, and the rest
report what they do not do). TxDrawD2D lays the text out with GDI as
TxDraw does, draws it twice into a bitmap, on black and on white, which
gives every pixel's coverage and premultiplied colour, and draws that
bitmap onto the Direct2D target, so text on a transparent background
keeps a transparent background.

Test: test/richtxsrv2-gate.sh with test/richtxsrv2-probe.c (mutants
SG_MUTANT_RICHED_NO_SERVICES2, SG_MUTANT_RICHED_NO_DOCUMENT2,
SG_MUTANT_RICHED_D2D_OPAQUE).
